---
description: Stationary-object evidence and conservative camera/Grok behavior
globs: vision/**,contracts/vision-*.json,contracts/vision-v1.md
alwaysApply: false
---

Read vision/AGENTS.md and contracts/vision-v1.md. Alan owns vision; mapping owns
metric transforms, backend owns durable state/authorization, robot owns DJI.
Never make stationary people or animals eligible. Living, carried and uncertain
subjects stay excluded. Pixels alone never prove metric stationarity.

Keep >=5 seconds AND >=10 metric observations, gap/age <=1 second, distance
<=0.05 m from the FIRST episode anchor and uncertainty <=0.025 m per sample.
Reset evidence on motion, staleness, identity/session/geometry/calibration changes.
Recheck evidence after async results; late Grok must not restore old eligibility.
An unprocessed newer frame prevents pickup eligibility. Potential targets are
review proposals, never permission to drive or pick up.

Keep detector numeric scores separate from qualitative Grok confidence.
Fixture outputs are labelled; missing XAI_API_KEY means UNAVAILABLE.
Only claim hardware/live API checks actually performed. Matching-frame lookup
returns the exact image or 404. Keep camera queues and external calls bounded.

Use vision/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q vision/tests from the repo root.
Read-only reviews and source-backed contract work can proceed while hardware
or peer credentials are pending. Never weaken a gate to make the demo appear ready.
